---
import { siteUrl } from '../../utils/site';
import Concept from '../../layouts/Concept.astro';
import Mermaid from '../../components/Mermaid.astro';
import SpeechBubbleMock from '../../components/screens/SpeechBubbleMock';

const chart = `flowchart LR
  Anchor["Node3D (live AABB top + 0.22m) or Vector3"] --> Proj["Camera3D project / off-screen bearing"]
  Proj --> Style["Resolve speaker pastel tint + tone shape"]
  Style --> Clamp["Float above actor, clamp viewport & HUD"]
  Clamp --> Arrow["Stretch pointer arrow (or cloud trail) back to speaker"]
`;
---

<Concept title="Speech Bubbles">
  <div class="diagram"><Mermaid chart={chart} /></div>

  <p>The key words <strong>MUST</strong>, <strong>MUST NOT</strong>, <strong>SHOULD</strong>, and <strong>MAY</strong> below are used as in RFC 2119.</p>

  <p>
    Non-blocking NPC and companion callouts — field companion reactions, the Guild Counter clerk's send-off,
    and Principal's Office quest briefings — share a single PSO-styled screen-space speech bubble component
    (<a href="https://github.com/kion-dgl/psz-godot/issues/557">issue #557</a>). Bubbles float comfortably above
    the action in PSO's forward-slanted silhouette with a solid black offset backdrop, per-character pastel tint,
    tone-adaptive contour, and a dynamic pointer arrow stretching back to the speaker.
  </p>

  <h2>Interactive PSO Shape, Speaker Color &amp; Placement Mock</h2>
  <p>
    Switch between PSO scenarios, character color swatches, and tone shapes (<strong>Normal</strong> slanted pill,
    <strong>Shout</strong> spiky burst, <strong>Thought</strong> cloud), or drag the orange head-anchor pin across
    HUD corners and off-screen edges.
  </p>
  <SpeechBubbleMock client:only="react" />

  <h2>PSO visual grammar: shape, black backdrop, and tone</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Normal (<code>normal</code>, default):</strong> A forward-slanted rounded parallelogram (<code>SLANT_RATIO = 0.26</code>, <code>18 px</code> rounded corners) with horizontal top and bottom edges and bold dark ink (<code>#080A10</code>, <code>JetBrainsMono-Bold.ttf</code> <code>15 px</code>). No inline speaker-name label is rendered inside the bubble — attribution comes from the character's pastel tint and the pointer arrow aimed directly at them.</li>
    <li><strong>Shout (<code>shout</code>):</strong> An angled spiky starburst perimeter with a stretching pointer spike aimed at the speaker, used for urgent battle warnings, ambushes, and exclaimed callouts (explicit <code>tone = "shout"</code> or <code>!!</code> lines under <code>auto</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Thought (<code>thought</code>):</strong> A scalloped cloud perimeter with three diminishing circular puffs stepping toward the speaker, used for quiet murmurs, hesitation, and internal asides (explicit <code>tone = "thought"</code> or parenthesized / leading-ellipsis murmurs under <code>auto</code>).</li>
    <li><strong>Solid black offset backdrop:</strong> Every bubble and tail/puff <strong>MUST</strong> draw a solid jet-black (<code>#000000</code>) duplicate silhouette offset by <code>(+6 px, +5 px)</code> behind the foreground fill, paired with a crisp dark hairline border so bright pastels pop cleanly against snow, sky, forest, and dark ruins alike.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Consistent per-character pastel palette</h2>
  <p>
    Named recurring characters <strong>MUST</strong> resolve to consistent high-luminance pastel fills so black text
    remains high-contrast while multi-speaker exchanges read at a glance:
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Speaker</th>
        <th>Hex</th>
        <th>Character tint</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Default / Town NPC</strong></td><td><code>#FFFFFF</code></td><td>Classic PSO crisp white</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Principal</strong></td><td><code>#F5F7FF</code></td><td>Cool ivory white</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Kai</strong></td><td><code>#FFF1BE</code></td><td>Warm hunter gold-cream</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Sarisa</strong></td><td><code>#FFDDF0</code></td><td>Soft Newman blossom pink</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Ogi</strong></td><td><code>#C6F3FF</code></td><td>PSO CAST ice cyan</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Elio</strong></td><td><code>#D6F7E2</code></td><td>Soft mint green</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Fern</strong></td><td><code>#E8F7C8</code></td><td>Meadow lime pastel</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Dr. Carlo</strong></td><td><code>#DAE7FF</code></td><td>Archive periwinkle blue</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Ren</strong></td><td><code>#CCF6F4</code></td><td>Soft aqua cyan</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Dorn</strong></td><td><code>#FFE4C8</code></td><td>Forge peach-amber</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Mira</strong></td><td><code>#EADBFF</code></td><td>Soft lavender</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Ana</strong></td><td><code>#EEF0FF</code></td><td>Moonlight pearl</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Vash</strong></td><td><code>#E2E8EE</code></td><td>Cool slate mist</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Floating placement, stretching tail, and off-screen directional arrow</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>All 3D-anchored speech bubbles <strong>MUST</strong> use <code>scripts/3d/ui/speech_bubble.gd</code> (<code>SpeechBubble</code>) on <code>CanvasLayer</code> layer <code>40</code> — above the 3D viewport (<code>0</code>) and below <code>SceneManager</code> overlays (<code>50</code>), map overlays (<code>100</code>), <a href={siteUrl('/states/start-menu')}>Start Menu</a> (<code>150</code>), <code>FieldHud</code> / <code>HudStats</code> (<code>200</code>), scene fade (<code>250</code>), and <a href={siteUrl('/states/crt-filter')}>CRT Filter</a> (<code>260</code>), allocating zero <code>SubViewport</code>s.</li>
    <li>When anchored to a <code>Node3D</code>, head height above <code>anchor.global_position</code> <strong>MUST</strong> be derived from static visual mesh bounds × world Y scale + <code>0.22 m</code> clearance (clamped to <code>[1.1 m, 2.4 m] + 0.22 m</code>, excluding <code>WeaponAttachment*</code> subtrees; <code>1.80 m + 0.22 m</code> fallback when unmeshed), including scaled actors such as the Principal (<code>0.09x</code> on the <code>1.05 m</code> <a href={siteUrl('/journey/city/office')}>Principal's Office</a> landing).</li>
    <li>Rather than sitting directly on the actor's forehead, the bubble body <strong>SHOULD</strong> float comfortably higher (<code>FLOAT_GAP = 86 px</code> above the head anchor when space allows) so the character and surrounding combat remain unobstructed, while the pointer tail stretches seamlessly down or diagonally to the speaker's head anchor.</li>
    <li>The bubble body <strong>MUST</strong> clamp inside safe viewport margins and nudge clear of active HUD corners (<code>HudStats</code>, <code>RoomMinimap</code>, <code>ActionPalette</code>, <code>TargetInfo</code>) and lower simultaneous bubbles.</li>
    <li>When the speaker is off-frame or behind the camera near plane, the bubble <strong>MUST</strong> clamp inside the safe frame and aim a directional arrow (up to <code>56 px</code>) back toward the screen edge or bottom bearing where the character's voice originates, never inverting across <code>w &lt; 0</code>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Implemented by</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>scripts/3d/ui/speech_bubble.gd</code> — shared PSO <code>SpeechBubble</code> layer, speaker palette, <code>normal</code> / <code>shout</code> / <code>thought</code> vector shapes with solid black backdrop, AABB head-offset resolver, and stretching/directional arrow solver.</li>
    <li><code>scripts/3d/elements/companion_npc.gd</code> — field companion reactions (<a href={siteUrl('/states/companion-combat')}>Companion Combat</a> speech hold preserved).</li>
    <li><code>scripts/3d/city/city_office_controller.gd</code> — Principal and quest-client multi-page briefing bubbles.</li>
    <li><code>scripts/3d/city/city_counter_controller.gd</code> — Guild Counter quest-accept send-off bubble.</li>
    <li><code>scripts/tools/speech_bubble_tests.gd</code> — deterministic unit tests (palette, tone shapes, AABB scale, clamping, directional arrows) and live 3D camera projection probe.</li>
  </ul>
</Concept>
